      "displayName": "Aaron Birkland",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Slug doesn't conflict with memento-datetime, so it isn't strictly necessary to remove it (i.e. Slug can remain an option, if the user wants to provide it) .  What the LDPRm resource is named (and how it appears in URIs) is cosmetic.  That being said, if it's advantageous to use a uniform naming scheme for mementos (i.e. to match the datetime, timestamp, or whatever), then go ahead and do it.</p>",
     "created": "22/Sep/17 5:02 PM",
     "id": "19376",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12563/comment/19376",
